<h3><a name="proposera" id="proposera">Proposal A Proposer</a></h3>
    <p>Sean Whitton [<a href="mailto:spwhitto@debian.org">spwhitto@debian.org</a>]
	[<a href='https://lists.debian.org/debian-vote/2024/06/msg00561.html'>text of proposal</a>]
	[<a href='https://lists.debian.org/debian-vote/2024/07/msg00025.html'>Withdrawal</a>]
    </p>
<h3><a name="secondsa" id="secondsa">Proposal A Seconds</a></h3>
    <ol>
        <li>Didier Raboud [<a href="mailto:odyx@debian.org">odyx@debian.org</a>] [<a href='https://lists.debian.org/debian-vote/2024/06/msg00562.html'>mail</a>]</li>
        <li>Jonathan McDowell [<a href="mailto:noodles@debian.org">noodles@debian.org</a>] [<a href='https://lists.debian.org/debian-vote/2024/06/msg00566.html'>mail</a>]</li>
        <li>Ian Jackson [<a href="mailto:iwj@debian.org">iwj@debian.org</a>] [<a href='https://lists.debian.org/debian-vote/2024/06/msg00568.html'>mail</a>]</li>
        <li>Aníbal Monsalve Salazar [<a href="mailto:anibal@debian.org">anibal@debian.org</a>] [<a href='https://lists.debian.org/debian-vote/2024/06/msg00571.html'>mail</a>]</li>
        <li>Sam Hartman [<a href="mailto:hartmans@debian.org">hartmans@debian.org</a>] [<a href='https://lists.debian.org/debian-vote/2024/06/msg00581.html'>mail</a>]</li>
        <li>Russ Allbery [<a href="mailto:rra@debian.org">rra@debian.org</a>] [<a href='https://lists.debian.org/debian-vote/2024/06/msg00585.html'>mail</a>]</li>
    </ol>
<h3><a name="texta" id="texta">Proposal A</a></h3>
<h3>Choice 1</h3>
<p>tag2upload allows DDs and DMs to upload simply by using the
git-debpush(1) script to push a signed git tag.</p>
<ol>
<li>tag2upload, in the form designed and implemented by Sean Whitton and
   Ian Jackson, and design reviewed by Jonathan McDowell and Russ
   Allbery, should be deployed to official Debian infrastructure.</li>
<li>Under Constitution §4.1(3), we overrule the ftpmaster delegate's
   decision: the Debian Archive should be configured to accept and trust
   uploads from the tag2upload service.</li>
<li>Future changes to tag2upload should follow normal Debian processes.</li>
<li>Nothing in this resolution should be taken as requiring maintainers
   to use any particular git or salsa workflows.</li>
</ol>
